WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.540
Happy Halloween!

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.120
It's that time of year when your neighbors
are secretly unwrapping candy,

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:26.400
and brushing lollipops with poison and inserting
razor blades into, pretty much everything.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.230
Actually, while it may be a Halloween tradition
to view your neighbors as psychopaths

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:34.790
who patiently wait for the one trite day of
the year to kill the local kids,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:39.700
in fact, no child has ever been killed by
a stranger's poisoned candy, ever.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.780
But you know what? facts don't stop fear.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.880
Here are 3 ways in which our misguided terror about Halloween is killing all the fun.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.360
Parents are so scared of letting their kids
roam free that, no joke,

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.700
there's now a thing called trunk or treat.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.840
Cars gather in a circle and kids go from one
trunk to the next to grab candy

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.370
as if walking around in a circle in a parking
lot and collecting sugar

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.380
is the whole point of the holiday.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.800
Yeah, sugar is important,

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:14.180
but so is going outside, with your friends,
on your own, at night.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:18.700
Some towns are so scared of the holiday that
they've placed curfews on trick-or-treating,

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.080
it's medieval, it's as if they really believe
that ghouls come out at night.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:32.859
There are schools, churches, community centers
sending home notes

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.960
begging parents not to let their kids wear
costumes that are too scary.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.540
As if kids can't handle an eyeball oozing
blood any more.

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:45.160
One town even made a guy take down his zombie
decorations in his front yard

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:47.600
because they were, quote: 'too realistic.'

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.800
In other words they looked too much like real
zombies?

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.760
In some towns, registered sex offenders have
to all gather together at the local precinct

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.260
like some twisted version of study hall.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:05.040
The rules are different in different places,

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.860
but they're all based on the idea that sex
offenders pounce on trick-or-treaters,

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.020
which, turns out to be, like the poison candy
story, completely false.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.860
There was a study done by a professor now
at Johns Hopkins

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:21.860
and she found that there is zero increase
in child sex offences on Halloween.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:27.180
In fact, the author Elizabeth Letourneau,
considered titling her study 'Halloween,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.640
the Safest Day of the Year.'

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.640
Because it is, when it comes to sex crimes.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.820
There's really just one thing to fear on Halloween and that's cars.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:40.780
More kids get hit by cars on Halloween than
any other day for obvious reasons.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:43.420
There are so many more kids outside.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.860
So if we really wanted to make the holiday
safer,

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:48.800
we would take off the cops who were watching
the sex offenders,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.840
and put them on traffic patrol instead.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.319
That could save some lives because cars are
actually dangerous,

00:02:56.319 --> 00:03:00.280
unlike a slightly torn Snickers bar.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.840
For Reason TV, I'm Lenore Skenazy.

